  "title": "Fake It or Mask It: Choosing the Right Data for Agent Simulation Environments",
  "description": "Agents need realistic worlds to train in, but the data behind them is rarely safe to use raw. Two paths dominate: synthetic data that mirrors production, or de-identified real data that keeps its messiness without exposing real people. Each makes different tradeoffs on fidelity, edge cases, governance, and generalization. Let's compare notes on where each shine, where it breaks, and where teams blend the two.\n\nSeating for this session is first-come, first-served. Add it to your schedule to plan your day and arrive early to secure a spot.",
